{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing f64 = double;\n\nconstexpr i64 LIMIT=1000005;\nconstexpr i64 M1=998244353;\nconstexpr i64 M2=1000000007;\nconstexpr i64 B=1000000;\n\ni64 N;\nvector<i64> V[10];\ni64 G;\ni64 S[10];\ni64 ANS;\n\nvoid precompute(i64 depth,i64 cur){\n    V[depth].emplace_back((++G-cur+M1)%M1);\n    S[depth]=(S[depth]+V[depth].back()%M2)%M2;\n    if(depth==6)return;\n    for(i64 digit=0;digit<=9;digit++) precompute(depth+1,cur*10+digit);\n}\n\nvoid explore(i64 val){\n    if(val>N)return;\n    if(val*B+B-1<=N && val*B*10>N){\n        i64 r=G;\n        for(i64 idx=0,pw=1;idx<=6;idx++,pw*=10){\n            i64 d=(r-val*pw)%M1;\n            if(d<0) d+=M1;\n            i64 pt=lower_bound(V[idx].begin(),V[idx].end(),-d+M1)-V[idx].begin();\n            i64 add=(d*(i64)V[idx].size()%M2+S[idx])%M2;\n            add=(add-((i64)V[idx].size()-pt)*M1%M2+M2)%M2;\n            ANS=(ANS+add)%M2;\n            G+=(i64)V[idx].size();\n        }\n        return;\n    }\n    ANS=(ANS+(++G-val+M1)%M1)%M2;\n    for(i64 d=0;d<=9;d++) explore(val*10+d);\n}\n\nint main(){\n#ifdef MYDEBUG\n    freopen(\"testdata.in\",\"r\",stdin);\n    freopen(\"test1.out\",\"w\",stdout);\n#endif\n    cin>>N;\n    precompute(0,0);\n    for(i64 k=0;k<=6;k++) sort(V[k].begin(),V[k].end());\n    G=0;\n    for(i64 s=1;s<=9;s++) explore(s);\n    cout<<ANS<<'\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    LIMIT = 1000005\n    M1 = 998244353\n    M2 = 1000000007\n    B = 1000000\n    \n    V = [[] for _ in range(10)]\n    G = 0\n    S = [0] * 10\n    ANS = 0\n\n    def precompute(depth, cur):\n        nonlocal G\n        G += 1\n        val = (G - cur) % M1\n        V[depth].append(val)\n        S[depth] = (S[depth] + val) % M2\n        if depth == 6:\n            return\n        for digit in range(10):\n            precompute(depth + 1, cur * 10 + digit)\n\n    def explore(val):\n        nonlocal G, ANS\n        if val > N:\n            return\n        if val * B + B - 1 <= N and val * B * 10 > N:\n            r = G\n            pw = 1\n            for idx in range(7):\n                d = (r - val * pw) % M1\n                if d < 0:\n                    d += M1\n                # Find lower bound for (-d + M1) in V[idx]\n                target = (-d + M1) % M1\n                pt = bisect.bisect_left(V[idx], target)\n                add = (d * len(V[idx]) + S[idx]) % M2\n                add = (add - (len(V[idx]) - pt) * M1) % M2\n                if add < 0:\n                    add += M2\n                ANS = (ANS + add) % M2\n                G += len(V[idx])\n                pw *= 10\n            return\n        G += 1\n        ANS = (ANS + (G - val) % M1) % M2\n        if ANS < 0:\n            ANS += M2\n        for d in range(10):\n       